Subject: [PATCH 08068/11362] [outer-loop] amend the QAT h2h pre-registration:
 exclusion reason was mischaracterised

The pre-registration said the 5 excluded games fail for "a property of the
fixtures independent of either arm's score". Measured, only ONE of five is:

  dc22  build_progress_window -> None      the documented "unsolvable to L1 offline"
  ka59  ValueError int('C:1')              unhandled coordinate-click action encoding
  sc25  AttributeError .hand_verifier      no registered GameAdapter
  tn36  same                               no registered GameAdapter
  wa30  same                               no registered GameAdapter

Four are harness limitations, not properties of the games.

Does NOT affect validity: all five fail before any LLM is invoked, so the
exclusion cannot favour either arm and the running 20-game extension is
unbiased.

DOES invalidate the stated stopping rule. "20 is the ceiling of this corpus" is
false; 20 is the ceiling of the current harness. Three adapters and one action
parser would reach 24 games. The revised rule keeps 20 as the last extension at
current tooling, but forbids describing the corpus as exhausted -- and forbids
deciding whether to raise the ceiling AFTER seeing the 20-game result, which
would be exactly the outcome-dependent stopping the pre-registration exists to
prevent.

Appended rather than edited, per never-prune.
